@startuml context-map
!pragma teoz true
title Context Map — {{System}}

' Canonical DDD notation (Vernon, *Implementing DDD* / Socoli):
'   U = Upstream (supplier),  D = Downstream (customer / consumer).
'   Influence flows  U --> D.  The pattern name sits at the upstream end.
'   Line style encodes the pattern (see legend). Edit names/relationships to fit the domain.

skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor<<core>>        LightYellow
  BackgroundColor<<supporting>>  White
  BackgroundColor<<generic>>     WhiteSmoke
  BackgroundColor<<mud>>         MistyRose
  BorderColor<<core>>            GoldenRod
  BorderColor<<mud>>             Crimson
  BorderThickness<<core>>        2
  BorderThickness<<mud>>         2
}
skinparam ArrowColor Black
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor White

' --- Contexts (stereotype = subdomain type; rename/replace to fit the domain) ---
rectangle "Sales\n(Core)"                    as Sales     <<core>>
rectangle "Catalog"                          as Catalog   <<supporting>>
rectangle "Inventory"                        as Inventory <<supporting>>
rectangle "Billing"                          as Billing   <<supporting>>
rectangle "Legacy ERP\n(Big Ball of Mud)"    as ERP       <<mud>>

' --- Relationships — Vernon's 9 patterns ---
' Customer-Supplier: U (Sales) supplies D (Billing / Inventory).
Sales     "U" --> "D"                  Billing    : Customer-Supplier
Sales     "U" --> "D"                  Inventory  : Customer-Supplier

' Conformist: D (Inventory) adopts U's (Catalog) model as-is. "C" marks the conformist end.
Catalog   "U" --> "D (C)"              Inventory  : Conformist

' Anticorruption Layer: D shields itself from a messy/legacy U. Dashed crimson, "ACL" at the D end.
ERP       "U" -[#crimson,dashed]-> "D (ACL)" Sales     : Anticorruption Layer
ERP       "U" -[#crimson,dashed]-> "D (ACL)" Catalog   : Anticorruption Layer

' --- Patterns not used in this example — copy/paste when needed ---
' Partnership (mutual, equal): gold double-headed arrow, "P" at both ends.
'   Sales "P" <-[#gold]-> "P" Partner : Partnership
' Shared Kernel (small shared subset): gold line, "SK" at both ends.
'   A "SK" -[#gold]-> "SK" B : Shared Kernel
' Open Host Service + Published Language: U exposes one open protocol + standard schema.
'   Upstream "U (OHS+PL)" --> "D" Downstream : OHS + Published Language
' Separate Ways: draw NO line — independence is the point. (Optionally add an "X" note.)

legend right
  |= Line style |= Pattern |
  | <color:#000000>────►</color>            | Customer–Supplier / Conformist |
  | <color:crimson>─ ─ ►</color>             | Anticorruption Layer (ACL) |
  | <color:gold>────►</color>               | Shared Kernel / Partnership |
  | (none)                                  | Separate Ways |
  |--
  Context box: <back:LightYellow> </back> Core  ·  <back:White> </back> Supporting  ·  <back:WhiteSmoke> </back> Generic  ·  <back:MistyRose> </back> Big Ball of Mud
endlegend

@enduml
